   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1795464289639,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "8. Cycles and how to break them",
   "originalText": "8. Cycles and how to break them",
   "fontSize": 30,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "el117_371764",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1979.3333333333333,
   "y": 2256.3,
   "width": 505.44,
   "height": 337.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 415849347,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1487179539,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1795464289639,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A cycle = A needs B and B needs A. Kahn gets stuck:\nboth keep indegree > 0 forever.\n\nExample: Author keeps vector<Book*> books,\n         Book keeps Author* author.\n\nFixes, best first:\n1. Make one side SOFT: in Author.h write `class Book;`\n   and only store Book* (no Book method calls there)\n2. Move the logic needing both into a higher layer\n   (a Manager / Service / Facade does it)\n3. Depend on an interface, not the concrete class\n   (dependency inversion)\n4. Header-only last resort: put that one method body\n   after both classes, or split into .h + .cpp",
   "originalText": "A cycle = A needs B and B needs A. Kahn gets stuck:\nboth keep indegree > 0 forever.\n\nExample: Author keeps vector<Book*> books,\n         Book keeps Author* author.\n\nFixes, best first:\n1. Make one side SOFT: in Author.h write `class Book;`\n   and only store Book* (no Book method calls there)\n2. Move the logic needing both into a higher layer\n   (a Manager / Service / Facade does it)\n3. Depend on an interface, not the concrete class\n   (dependency inversion)\n4. Header-only last resort: put that one method body\n   after both classes, or split into .h + .cpp",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
