   "locked": false,
   "text": "11. Layer rules",
   "originalText": "11. Layer rules",
   "fontSize": 30,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "el172_300599",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1356,
   "y": 3256.3,
   "width": 570.96,
   "height": 382.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 594674889,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 90621425,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1795464289639,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "• A file may #include only from its own layer or a lower one\n• Never include upward (a model must never include a manager)\n• Inside a layer, follow the topological order\n• Layer = ROLE (which way includes may point).\n  Level = EARLIEST a class can be written (from the graph).\n  A Manager is role L8 but may be level 3: it can be written\n  early, it just must never be included by anything below L8.\n• Folders group by role; the build order can cross folders:\n  an abstract base in models/ may need an interface from\n  strategies/, so that interface is written first\n• Memory hooks:\n  interface before implementation\n  part before whole\n  parent before child\n  product before its factory\n  item before its manager\n  everything before the facade, facade before main",
   "originalText": "• A file may #include only from its own layer or a lower one\n• Never include upward (a model must never include a manager)\n• Inside a layer, follow the topological order\n• Layer = ROLE (which way includes may point).\n  Level = EARLIEST a class can be written (from the graph).\n  A Manager is role L8 but may be level 3: it can be written\n  early, it just must never be included by anything below L8.\n• Folders group by role; the build order can cross folders:\n  an abstract base in models/ may need an interface from\n  strategies/, so that interface is written first\n• Memory hooks:\n  interface before implementation\n  part before whole\n  parent before child\n  product before its factory\n  item before its manager\n  everything before the facade, facade before main",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
